1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,140
Size matters on the wire.

2
00:00:03,880 --> 00:00:05,660
Too large to pass.

3
00:00:07,440 --> 00:00:09,180
Too quiet to fail.

4
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:12,800
The packet waits.

5
00:00:23,280 --> 00:00:24,200
M-T-U at the edge of the frame,

6
00:00:24,560 --> 00:00:26,540
one byte too heavy and nothing feels the same.

7
00:00:26,920 --> 00:00:28,160
Payload loaded, header tight,

8
00:00:28,560 --> 00:00:29,700
trying to cross the path tonight.

9
00:00:30,880 --> 00:00:31,940
D-F bit says do not break,

10
00:00:31,940 --> 00:00:33,240
no fragment left for the route to take.

11
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:35,300
Silent drop in the middle lane,

12
00:00:35,640 --> 00:00:37,020
users only feel the pain.

13
00:00:37,020 --> 00:00:37,960
Ping goes through,

14
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:38,600
large one dies.

15
00:00:38,940 --> 00:00:39,840
Small test passes,

16
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:40,360
truth still hides.

17
00:00:40,660 --> 00:00:41,540
Trace the path,

18
00:00:41,760 --> 00:00:42,120
lower the size,

19
00:00:42,540 --> 00:00:43,700
watch the hidden fault arise.

20
00:00:49,340 --> 00:00:49,860
M-T-U.

21
00:00:49,860 --> 00:00:50,880
Can you pass it through?

22
00:00:52,520 --> 00:00:53,040
M-T-U.

23
00:00:53,120 --> 00:00:54,380
The packet knows the truth.

24
00:00:54,980 --> 00:00:56,440
Too big to ride,

25
00:00:56,980 --> 00:00:57,460
too small to see,

26
00:00:58,080 --> 00:00:59,900
find the path.

27
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:00,900
where the frame runs free.

28
00:01:01,580 --> 00:01:02,500
Don't fragment.

29
00:01:02,760 --> 00:01:03,980
Can't fragment.

30
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:07,040
Path too narrow.

31
00:01:08,280 --> 00:01:08,700
Packet stranded.

32
00:01:08,700 --> 00:01:09,320
Don't fragment.

33
00:01:09,320 --> 00:01:09,600
Can't fragment.

34
00:01:12,460 --> 00:01:14,400
Lower the size.

35
00:01:14,860 --> 00:01:15,600
Understand it.

36
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:17,460
Tunnel overhead, labels in line,

37
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:19,680
encapsulation stealing bytes in time.

38
00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:20,840
V-P-N wraps it, M-P-L-S too,

39
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:23,440
suddenly the old size will not do.

40
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:25,020
Discovery tries to read the road,

41
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:26,940
ICMP should carry the code.

42
00:01:27,240 --> 00:01:28,120
If the message never comes back,

43
00:01:28,720 --> 00:01:30,520
M-T-U becomes the crack.

44
00:01:30,520 --> 00:01:31,500
Fourteen hundred.

45
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:32,840
Fifteen hundred.

46
00:01:33,740 --> 00:01:34,960
Jumbo frame.

47
00:01:34,960 --> 00:01:36,340
Do not fragment.

48
00:01:36,740 --> 00:01:38,920
Path M-T-U.

49
00:01:38,920 --> 00:01:40,320
ICMP too big.

50
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:44,360
Reduce and retry.

51
00:01:45,700 --> 00:01:46,500
M-T-U.

52
00:01:46,860 --> 00:01:47,920
Can you pass it through?

53
00:01:49,240 --> 00:01:50,040
M-T-U.

54
00:01:50,040 --> 00:01:51,260
The packet knows the truth.

55
00:01:51,860 --> 00:01:52,760
Too big to ride,

56
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:54,520
too small to see,

57
00:01:54,960 --> 00:01:56,760
find the path.

58
00:01:56,760 --> 00:01:57,800
where the frame runs free.
